spicexplorer-gmid
=================

This package is MIT-licensed, consistent with the rest of the SpiceXplorer platform.

Third-party dependencies (not vendored — installed from PyPI)
-----------------------------------------------------------

  * **pygmid** (https://github.com/dreoilin/pygmid) — used as the lookup-table *reader*: the
    ``Lookup`` class loads the committed ``.pkl`` LUTs and performs the multilinear bias
    interpolation + the GM_ID ratio cross-lookups. Only its reader is used; its Spectre-only
    table *sweeper* is not (our LUTs are generated by the analog-db ``gmid-extract`` ngspice
    decks). pygmid is a normal runtime dependency, never copied into this tree.

  * **numpy** — grid/sweep array math.

Methodology reference (no code derived)
--------------------------------------

The sizing flows implement the gm/ID lookup-table methodology of Jespers & Murmann,
*Systematic Design of Analog CMOS Circuits Using Pre-Computed Lookup Tables* (Cambridge, 2017),
and Murmann's *Book-on-gm-ID-design* companion material. The methodology (the lookup/de-normalize
recipe, the saturation/fT/gain sanity gates) is encoded; no book source file is included. The
agent-facing condensation lives in the meta-repo ``.claude/skills/gmid-skills/``.
